{"content":[{"c":["BIZIOTHIAH, BIZJOTHJAH*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Listed in ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.28","r":"Josh.15.28","rawR":"Josh.15.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.28","value":"Josh.15.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Joshua 15:28"}," (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “Bizjothjah”) as a city in the Negev Desert area of Judah. The Greek OT, called the Septuagint, has “and her daughters,” which would mean that this was not a specific place but rather the cluster of villages surrounding Hazar-shual and Beersheba. Such a translation is possible with a slight adjustment to the Hebrew text. It is difficult to say how the Hebrew text originally read."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BiziothiahBizjothjah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Joshua 15:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.28","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.28","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.28"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"4329718f716d28a0ca3f987f1cfbedc3dab64558b04505d1362a7817a3beb61e","sourceItemName":"BiziothiahBizjothjah","sourceItemOrder":338,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BiziothiahBizjothjah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Biziothiah, Bizjothjah*","title":"Biziothiah, Bizjothjah*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}